============================
HTTP/1.1 201 Created
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Location: /ngsi-ld/v1/entities/urn:V2
Link: REGEX(.*)
Content-Length: 0




03. Seed urn:V3 (color=green)
=============================
HTTP/1.1 201 Created
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Location: /ngsi-ld/v1/entities/urn:V3
Link: REGEX(.*)
Content-Length: 0




04. Seed urn:V4 (color=blue) — second blue, expect both in filtered map
=======================================================================
HTTP/1.1 201 Created
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Location: /ngsi-ld/v1/entities/urn:V4
Link: REGEX(.*)
Content-Length: 0




05a. Create EntityMap with q=color=="blue" — page 1 = V2 + V4 only
===================================================================
     Response is page 1 of the filtered set; the map being created
     is the filtered set, NOT the universe of Vehicles.
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
NGSILD-EntityMap: REGEX(.*)
Link: REGEX(.*)
Content-Length: 245

[
  {
    "color": {
      "type": "Property",
      "value": "blue"
    },
    "id": "urn:V2",
    "type": "Vehicle"
  },
  {
    "color": {
      "type": "Property",
      "value": "blue"
    },
    "id": "urn:V4",
    "type": "Vehicle"
  }
]



05b. Capture the EntityMap id from the same request (separate call)
===================================================================
Map captured (id present): yes


06. GET /entityMaps/<id> — map's entryList holds V2 + V4 only
=============================================================
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Link: REGEX(.*)
Content-Length: 230

{
  "entityMap": {
    "urn:V2": [
      "@none"
    ],
    "urn:V4": [
      "@none"
    ]
  },
  "expiresAt": "REGEX(.*)",
  REGEX(.*EntityMap.*),
  "linkedMaps": {},
  "type": "EntityMap"
}



07. Paginate same map without any filter — V2 + V4 (the frozen filtered set)
============================================================================
    Map fixes the source mapping; filters from create-time are NOT remembered.
    But the map's entry set is already only V2 + V4 (red+green never made it in).
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Link: REGEX(.*)
Content-Length: 245

[
  {
    "color": {
      "type": "Property",
      "value": "blue"
    },
    "id": "urn:V2",
    "type": "Vehicle"
  },
  {
    "color": {
      "type": "Property",
      "value": "blue"
    },
    "id": "urn:V4",
    "type": "Vehicle"
  }
]



08. Paginate same map with q=color=="red" — empty
=================================================
    Map only contains V2 + V4 (blue); current request's q filters that to nothing.
    Filter narrows; it cannot re-introduce V1 (red) — the map froze it out.
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Link: REGEX(.*)
Content-Length: 3

[]



--TEARDOWN--
swBrokerStop
swDbDrop
